# Tranco Top 1 Million List

This directory contains the Tranco Top 1 Million domain list used as an auxiliary input in the controlled generation of benign DNS and DNS over HTTPS traffic for the UFU-Do53-EXF and UFU-DoH-EXF datasets.

The Tranco ranking is a research-oriented top-sites list designed to provide a more stable and manipulation-resistant alternative to traditional website popularity rankings.

The list was used to define a documented and repeatable source of domain names for the benign traffic-generation scenarios.

---

# Directory contents

```text
scripts/Tranco List/
├── top-1m.csv
└── README.md
```

## `top-1m.csv`

The file contains:

- 1,000,000 domain names;
- one domain per row;
- no header row;
- one text column;
- domains ordered according to the corresponding Tranco ranking.

Example:

```text
google.com
mail.ru
microsoft.com
facebook.com
apple.com
```

---

# Role in the dataset methodology

The Tranco list was used to support the controlled generation of benign traffic for both datasets:

- **UFU-Do53-EXF**, using conventional DNS queries;
- **UFU-DoH-EXF**, using DNS over HTTPS requests.

The use of a documented ranking reduces arbitrary domain selection and improves the repeatability of the benign traffic-generation procedure.

The list was not used as a security reputation database.

A domain appearing in Tranco must not automatically be interpreted as:

- benign;
- trustworthy;
- safe;
- free of malicious content;
- suitable for unrestricted access.

The ranking is based primarily on popularity and ranking methodology, not on cybersecurity reputation.